<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Order of Saint Stephen (Tuscany)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1561">1561</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Order of Saint Stephen Pope and Martyr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Order of Saint Stephen is a Tuscan military order of knights founded in 1561 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a> and based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">galleys</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> corsairs in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, joined the Christian fleet at Lepanto in 1571 and raided the North African coast. It was abolished in 1859 and later survived as a dynastic order.</p></div>
